Technical Specification: Spaceware – Proxima Descent (Version 3)

Surface Exploration Transition & Resource Gathering

1. Objective

Transform the landing cutscene into a seamless cinematic transition that changes the game genre from "descent survival" to "surface exploration tycoon".

The player must feel they are watching a movie that suddenly becomes interactive again.


2. Trigger Condition

The transition starts when:

· altitude == 0 (landing achieved)
· The landing cutscene animation is complete (ship on ground, dust settled)

No user input required. The transition is automatic.

3. Cinematic Letterbox Effect

When the transition begins:

· Black bars slide in from top and bottom.
· Bar height: 15% of screen height each.
· Animation duration: 0.5 seconds, smooth slide (ease-in-out).
· Bars remain visible during the entire surface exploration phase (they never disappear).

Purpose: Signal to the player that the game has entered a "cinematic mode". The astronaut is now the protagonist of a survival film.

4. Ship-to-Astronaut Transformation

4.1 Ship Fade Out

· The Janax-M1 spacecraft fades out over 1 second (opacity 1 → 0).
· No explosion. No debris. Just a smooth disappearance.

4.2 Astronaut Instantiation

· At the exact moment the ship reaches opacity 0, an astronaut SVG appears at the same position.
· Initial opacity: 0.

4.3 Astronaut Fade In

· Astronaut fades in over 0.5 seconds (opacity 0 → 1).

4.4 Astronaut Specifications

Attribute Value
Style White wireframe SVG, no fill, stroke width 2
Shape Helmet, torso, backpack, two arms, two legs (simplified geometric)
Size Same as the ship (approx 5% of screen width)
Position Ground level (bottom third of screen)
Animation Idle: slight breathing (scale 1.0 → 1.02 → 1.0, cycle 2s)

5. HUD Transformation

The HUD must change completely. No remnants of the descent phase.

5.1 Remove Descent HUD

· Altitude counter: hidden (no longer relevant)
· Integrity bar: hidden (ship is gone)

5.2 Add Surface Exploration HUD

Resource counters (top left):

Resource Icon (SVG) Initial Value
Scrap Gear icon 0
Food Apple/leaf icon 0
Artifacts Diamond / alien relic icon 0

Additional HUD elements (top right):

· Oxygen bar (reserved for future versions, but placeholder shown as 100%)
· Time on surface (optional, not required for V3)


6. Resource Spawning System

Once gamePhase = "SURFACE_EXPLORATION" is set:

6.1 Spawn Rules

· Resources spawn randomly on the ground level (same Y coordinate as the astronaut).
· Spawn rate: 1 resource every 3–5 seconds.
· Maximum resources on screen at once: 5 (to prevent clutter).
· Resources disappear if not collected within 15 seconds.

6.2 Resource Types & Behaviors

Resource Color (SVG stroke) Collection Effect
Scrap White +1 to Scrap counter
Food Green +1 to Food counter
Artifacts Cyan +1 to Artifacts counter, triggers a scientific fact (see 7.1)

6.3 Collection Mechanism

· The astronaut does not move left/right (yet). Collection is click/tap on the resource.
· When clicked: resource disappears, counter increments, sound effect (bleep).

7. Educational Component (Light)

7.1 Artifact Discovery

· Whenever the player collects an Artifact, a scientific fact appears at the bottom of the screen for 3 seconds.
· Fact content: Random from a list of 10 pre-defined facts about Proxima Centauri B (temperature, atmosphere, potential habitability, etc.).
· Fact box: White wireframe rectangle, black background, monospace font.

7.2 Fact List (example)

```
"Proxima Centauri B orbits its star every 11.2 days."
"Surface temperature: -39°C (cold, but potential liquid water under ice)."
"The star Proxima Centauri is a red dwarf, much dimmer than our Sun."
"Tidal locking means one side always faces the star."
```

8. Game State Management

8.1 Phase Variable

Add a global variable gamePhase with possible values:

· "DESCENT" (V1)
· "LANDING_CUTSCENE" (V2)
· "SURFACE_EXPLORATION" (V3 – this version)

8.2 Resource Variables

```typescript
let scrapCount = 0;
let foodCount = 0;
let artifactsCount = 0;
```

8.3 Spawn Timer

Use setInterval or a game loop with delta time:

```javascript
let spawnTimer = 0;
const SPAWN_INTERVAL = 4000; // milliseconds

// In game loop:
spawnTimer += deltaTime;
if (spawnTimer >= SPAWN_INTERVAL && resourceCount < 5) {
    spawnResource();
    spawnTimer = 0;
}
```

9. Visual Aesthetic (Surface Phase)

Element Specification
Background Black void (same as descent) – silence and emptiness amplifies isolation
Ground A single white horizontal line at bottom third (Y = 0.7 * screen height)
Stars Optional: a few static white dots (no animation)
Resources Simple wireframe icons, no fill, white/colored stroke
Letterbox bars Black, 15% top + 15% bottom, static after slide-in

10. Integration with V1 and V2

Version Phase What happens
V1 Descent 40,000 → 0 altitude, avoid asteroids
V2 Landing cutscene Ship lands, dust, tilt, text
V3 Surface exploration Astronaut appears, collect resources, discover facts

The transition must be seamless. No loading screens. No abrupt cuts. The letterbox slide and ship fade happen simultaneously, creating a single fluid motion.

11. Deliverable

A functional Rezona game that:

1. Completes the descent phase (V1)
2. Plays the landing cutscene (V2)
3. Automatically transitions to surface exploration with:
   · Letterbox black bars (slide-in)
   · Ship fade out + astronaut fade in
   · Resource counters (Scrap, Food, Artifacts)
   · Random resource spawning on ground
   · Click/tap collection
   · Artifact facts (educational)
4. No user input required for the transition (after landing cutscene ends)

12. Success Metrics for V3

Metric Target
Transition smoothness No visible glitches, no frame drops
Resource spawn & collection Works 100% of the time
Educational facts Player sees at least 1 fact per 3 artifacts
Player understanding No instructions needed; player discovers collection by clicking

